# Sobelow (Phoenix security scanner) - `mix sobelow --config`, run by precommit and CI.
#
# Reviewed false positives are skipped INLINE, with a `# sobelow_skip ["Category.Name"]`
# comment directly above the function (or pipeline) that holds the finding. They
# travel with the code, so an edit above them cannot unsuppress them (the old
# line-based fingerprint file could, and did). `skip: true` is what makes
# Sobelow read those comments. Every one was read in context:
#   * Traversal.* - paths are built by the app (its data dir, temp files, a
#     bundled catalogue) or looked up by id in the app's own listing before they
#     are touched; no request string is ever joined into a path.
#     (`Alnasl.HallReplays` writes where a developer's own `mix alnasl.hall pin`
#     tells it to, which is the point.)
#     (`mix fair_play.power --out FILE` likewise: the operator's own file.)
#     (`mix fair_play.dump`, `fair_play.fit`/`check`/`label` outputs: the same.)
#     (`AlnaslWeb.SupportController` reads Plug's own temp file of a multipart upload.)
#     (`Alnasl.Ops.OffsiteBackup` works in `<data dir>/offsite` on names it makes
#     itself; `Alnasl.Ops.Age`'s file functions are given those, or the
#     operator's own paths by `mix ops.age`.)
#     (`Alnasl.AccessPin` and `Alnasl.PinRequest` touch two fixed names in the data
#     dir; the request file's contents are a PIN, never a path.)
#     (`Alnasl.Takeover.Replica` writes `<data dir>/litestream.yml` and works in
#     `<data dir>/replica-restore` on names it makes itself; the box uid that
#     goes into the replica URL is regex-checked and never becomes a path here.)
#   * XSS.* - bodies are fixed SVG/PDF/ndjson/escaped-HTML builders, release notes through Alnasl.Markdown (allowlisted tags) or the app's own
#     bundled manual; content types are literals.
#   * DOS.StringToAtom - atoms come from the app's own literals, bundled data or a
#     regex-bounded letter set, never from a request.
#   * CI.System - fixed commands with an argument list (no shell string).
#     (`Alnasl.Takeover.Replica.Litestream` runs the operator's ALNASL_LITESTREAM,
#     accepted only as an absolute path to an existing file named litestream,
#     else `litestream` from the PATH; fixed subcommand and flags, no shell.)
#   * Config.CSP - no script-src policy is set; Phoenix's default
#     put_secure_browser_headers is on the browser pipeline. Reported, not fixed:
#     it listens on localhost / behind the operator's own access layer only.
#     (Skipped inline above each `pipeline` in the router.)
#   * Config.CSRF - the /join JSON endpoint is called by a bridge program, not a
#     browser: the one-time code in the body is the credential, there is no
#     session to forge. (Skipped inline above its `pipeline`.)
#
# Two checks cannot take an inline comment (Sobelow reads their finding from
# config files, not from a function), so they are ignored by name below:
#   * Config.CSWH - the socket origin is checked in config (check_origin).
#   * Config.HTTPS - TLS is not ours to enable: the app listens on localhost or
#     behind the operator's own access layer (tunnel / reverse proxy) that
#     terminates it.
[
  exit: :low,
  format: "txt",
  ignore: ["Config.CSWH", "Config.HTTPS"],
  ignore_files: [],
  include_mix_tasks: false,
  include_scripts: false,
  out: nil,
  private: false,
  router: nil,
  skip: true,
  summary: false,
  threshold: :low,
  verbose: false
]
